pool.help=How the pool deduplicates agents\n----------------------------------------\nThe pool keeps at most one live agent process per identity key. Two acquires whose\nkey matches on ALL of the following reuse the same process (a shared client);\nany difference forks a separate process:\n  \u2022 agentId             \u2014 the resolved registry id of the agent\n  \u2022 startConfig         \u2014 fingerprint of command / baseArgs / args / env / workingDir\n  \u2022 cwd                 \u2014 the project working directory (exact path, no canonicalization)\n  \u2022 eelDescriptor       \u2014 the execution environment (local, WSL, Docker, \u2026)\n\nEach chat thread that uses a client holds a lease; the process is stopped when the\nlast lease is released. Select a client on the left to see its state, pid, uptime\nand the exact key that identifies it.

